.TH YT-DLP-ARIA2-DOWNLOADER 1 "" "yt-dlp aria2 downloader" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yt-dlp-aria2-downloader \- download one video or audio track with managed yt-dlp and aria2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yt-dlp-aria2-downloader
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " VIDEO_URL"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yt-dlp-aria2-downloader
is the command-line engine for yt-dlp aria2 downloader. It downloads one URL
as a complete MKV video or as the best available native audio track. Direct
HTTP(S) media may use aria2; DASH and HLS remain on yt-dlp's native downloader.
yt-dlp and Deno are managed in per-user runtime storage and verified before use.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -o ", " --output-dir " " DIR
Write the final media into DIR.
.TP
.BR -m ", " --mode " " MODE
Select
.B video
or
.BR audio .
Video mode produces a complete MKV. Audio mode preserves the source codec and
container whenever possible.
.TP
.B --machine-progress
Emit stable machine-readable plan and progress records.
.TP
.B --youtube-hls-firefox
For YouTube video mode, read Firefox cookies and use the authenticated HLS
fallback before remuxing to MKV.
.TP
.B --tracks-auto
For compatible video sources, prefer reliably identified original audio.
Otherwise choose French, then the site's default or another ordinary audio
track, and report that the original version is unknown. For the selected default
audio, choose no subtitles when French, or full French subtitles for another
known language when uniquely available. Otherwise select no subtitles and
explain why. Forced subtitles never replace a full translation.
.TP
.B --all-tracks
For compatible video sources, select all distinct admissible audio and subtitle
tracks after filtering and deduplication. Hearing-impaired subtitles and
explicitly identified comfort audio are excluded. Audio description remains a
separate available category. Publish one validated MKV without re-encoding
audio or video.
.TP
.B --no-subtitles
Select audio automatically with no subtitle tracks. Also combine with
--tracks-auto or --all-tracks to retain that audio choice without subtitles.
.TP
.B --track-catalog " " FILE
Publish a private track catalogue and wait for --track-selection.
This structured handoff is used by the GUI within the same engine session.
.TP
.B --track-selection " " FILE
Read a private JSON selection bound to the current track catalogue. Excluded,
missing or stale track selections fail before media transfer.
.TP
.B --result-file " " FILE
Write the final media path to FILE.
.TP
.B --url-file " " FILE
Read the single URL from a private regular file instead of a positional
argument. The file must be owned by the current user and inaccessible to group
and other users.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display command help.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Display the program version.
.SH TRACK SELECTION
Audio and subtitle choices are independent. The output contains one video and
exactly the selected tracks. Subtitles remain selectable in the player.
Full translations and forced subtitles for selected passages are distinct.
UTF-8 SRT preserves text, line breaks and timing; source positioning is not
retained. Unsupported formatting or timing causes an explicit error.
Availability depends on the programme, territory and rights. A missing selected
track is never silently replaced, and a changed selection cannot resume
incompatible partial files.
.SH SHARED DESTINATIONS
Independent GUI and CLI instances may transfer and process media concurrently
in the same folder. Final files appear directly there. Overlapping filename
families are refused with status 75; existing final files or unowned native
inputs are preserved with status 1. No numeric suffix is added automatically.
.PP
Reservations cover the same user and host, including canonical path aliases.
They remain held through consumer shutdown and cleanup. Native resume requires
an unchanged ownership checkpoint from a confirmed stop; a .part name alone is
insufficient. Uncertain shutdown preserves active state for manual inspection.
A verified filesystem identity separates a recreated directory from an older
checkpoint when its inode number is reused. Missing identity information does
not authorize releasing an older active checkpoint.
Do not delete old-looking lock files. The shared legacy lock excludes an older
2.3.29 instance's exclusive lock. This is not distributed exclusion and does
not cover arbitrary external writers.
.SH PROCESS SUPERVISION
Linux pidfds, WNOWAIT and readable process/thread inventories in procfs are
required in addition to Bash 4.4 and Python 3.10. The application checks their
operation on a private disposable child before media work; unavailable
capabilities cause an early refusal with status 69. A later observation or
permission failure preserves resources and does not establish complete shutdown.
A zombie thread leader with live sibling threads is still an active consumer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/yt-dlp-aria2-downloader/
Default per-user data and managed runtime location when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is not set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp-aria2-downloader-gui (1),
.BR yt-dlp (1),
.BR aria2c (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/OscarFrog/yt-dlp-aria2-downloader-gui
